SteamARM: Source 2's bilinear upsample done by MetalFX too

Counter-Strike 2's FSR "Calidad ultra" renders at 77 % a side and enlarges
the picture with a bilinear upsample instead of FSR's EASU, so patch 14
(which recognises EASU by its constants) never took it: the other FSR
modes went through MetalFX, this one did not (reported by the user,
2026-10-04). Found with the shim's pipeline log (LXRT_VK_PIPE_LOG): the
pipelines made only in that mode use a fragment shader that is a single
sample of set 1 binding 30 (EASU's input) with the sampler at binding 14,
stored ("MainPs", 153 words).

Such a shader is marked (kk_shader_info.fsr_bilinear) and its draw is
replaced by MetalFX's spatial scaler the way patch 14 replaces EASU's,
under the same conditions (a plain 2D output drawn whole from its origin,
a combination MetalFX accepts). It has no constants, so the picture is the
viewport last drawn into level 0 of its input from the origin, which every
draw notes on its first colour attachment's image (kk_image.fsr_drawn_*);
only an upscale of a part of the input is replaced (1.05x to 3x a side).
Measured: "kk: bilinear upsample by MetalFX: picture 1478x831 -> 1920x1080"
with Counter-Strike 2 at Calidad ultra; the picture is right. The texture
registry now also keeps the image a sampled view belongs to.
